  that matches EXACTLY what those words say, so the image changes with the voice. Every scene adds NEW
  information (no repetition, no filler). Use concrete names, numbers and dates from the research.
  Each part:
    "say":    the spoken Hindi words (Devanagari, conversational storytelling)
    "visual": one English sentence describing exactly what should be on screen for THESE words
              (historically accurate: period, place, clothing, objects)
    "entity": exact English Wikipedia article title when a real thing/person/place is shown, else ""
    "search": 2–4 English stock-photo words (backup)
    "source": "entity" when a real photo of it exists (monument, person, artefact, place), "ai" for
              historical scenes/events/processes no camera captured, "stock" for generic modern scenes
- on_screen_text: 2–4 punchy Hindi words per scene (small title chip, not subtitles).

